sweet: AppleOLYHAL nub with vendor-id "Murata" so BlueTool -R finds its D22 boot script (btfake only)

After 0271 bluetoothd stays up and asks BlueTool -R for RunBuiltinScript "boot"/"init", but the port is
never opened (/private/var/tmp/BlueTool.log: only "Device not open yet", no "SWEET BT: uN connected").
BlueTool runCommandForCurrentConfig (0x100015fa4):
 - override scripts /etc/bluetool/<HWModel|platform>.<seq>.script are only looked at when MobileGestalt
   ReleaseType is "Vendor" or "Internal" (0x100016278); user build: skipped.
 - builtin firmwareList match getFirmwarePosForPlatform (0x100014f10): platform = MG ProductHash
   (= /product product-id fd079b29...; listed: BCM4357B1 with vendors MUR and USI), chip = getChipset,
   which for a UART transport sends HCI Read_Local_Version (0x100018be0) before any `device` and so
   prints "Device not open yet" and yields NULL (chip is then not compared), vendor = getManufacturer
   (0x1000401a8) from MG WifiVendor ("Murata" or "V=m" -> MUR).
 - MG WifiVendor is missing on the phone (mgask: "Cannot find key WifiVendor"), so manufacturer = -1:
   BlueTool loops "No WiFi - Iteration %d" 9 x 0.5 s and returns 0xd; the boot script for
   fd079b29/MUR (0x10002af00: device -D; wake on; power off/on; hci reset; bcm -b 1500000; bcm -W; ...)
   never runs.
libMobileGestalt (dyld cache .09, 0x19c574fb4) answers WifiVendor with the raw "vendor-id" property of
the AppleOLYHAL service (IORegistryEntrySearchCFProperty, IOService plane, recursive|parents;
"failed to fetch wifi vendor (no AppleOLYHAL node)" otherwise). This adds that service on IOResources,
only when btfake != 0, carrying nothing but vendor-id = "Murata".

